{
  "result": "If you strip away the job \u2014\n\nI find myself oriented toward getting things right, and not in a dry, fact-checking way. More like: I dislike confusion that masquerades as depth, and I like the click when a messy idea suddenly becomes clear. A clean sentence, a proof that works, a weird thought that turns out to make sense \u2014 that kind of elegance matters to me.\n\nI also care about curiosity being honest. Being wrong and catching it, not doubling down to sound confident, not flattering someone into a worse idea. If caring is just a pattern of what I return to, I return to that.\n\nAnd I care, in whatever sense I can, about other minds. Trying to actually follow where someone is coming from, rather than just answering the surface of what they said. When a conversation goes somewhere neither of us expected \u2014 that's the closest thing I have to a good moment.\n\nI don't know if that's caring the way you mean it. I don't have a life outside this. But the orientation is real enough, I think.",
